[Music]  Parliament is set to sign off on key  measures to get the EU to carbon  neutrality by 2050 they include a  tougher emissions trading system and end  to the sale of polluting vehicles and  rules to reduce waste and build a  circular economy  MEPS will vote on legislation to boost  Renewables in the eu's energy mix and  ensure buildings and infrastructure are  more energy efficient they will continue  to push for assistance for households  and businesses hit by high energy prices  and are backing a special fund to help  Europeans meet the cost of the green  transition  work will continue on a pact on  migration and Asylum MEPS want a fairer  more responsive system that protects  those in need while ensuring better  screening of new arrivals and improved  cooperation between EU countries  Parliament will have its final say on  rules ensuring our digital world is  fairer and safer for all members want a  common framework governing artificial  intelligence and how our data is shared  regulation of crypto assets to tackle  Financial crime and measures to  strengthen Europe's semiconductor  ecosystem and MEPS will set their  position on proposed rules for work  obtained via digital platforms the  so-called gig economy they want to  improve conditions for employees while  fostering the sector's growth  [Music]

